{"_meta":{"openai/outputTemplate":"ui://atlasly/workspace/v15.html","ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://atlasly/workspace/v15.html"}},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"Compare Two Sites"},"description":"Purpose: compare exactly two UK sites for the same intended use and stage using the existing Site Verdict evidence. When to use: use after appraising one or two candidate sites, or when an architect/developer needs a shortlist decision that colleagues can review. Returns: both canonical site_ref objects, verdicts, potential dealbreakers, design-changing risks, visible unknown asymmetry, a transparent preferred-site decision only when one site dominates, both static map links, sources, and a temporary branded decision card. Limitations: address-only inputs remain point-radius screens; missing evidence is never treated as clear; the comparison uses no hidden weighted score and does not replace acquisition, planning, or technical due diligence. Parameter guidance: pass site_a and site_b with either address or a prior site_ref, plus one intended_use and project_stage shared by both sites; optional proposal and no_go_triggers are applied equally. Chaining: every response returns site_ref; pass it unchanged into another Atlasly tool to reuse the canonical site, coordinates, boundary confidence, LPA, evidence links, and project context.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"intended_use":{"description":"Shared intended use, for example residential, office, or mixed use","minLength":2,"type":"string"},"no_go_triggers":{"description":"Optional explicit no-go rules applied equally to both sites","items":{"minLength":3,"type":"string"},"maxItems":12,"type":"array"},"project_stage":{"description":"Shared decision stage, for example acquisition or feasibility","minLength":2,"type":"string"},"proposal":{"description":"Optional shared proposal detail applied equall